  :adr/decision-summary
  "{:trigger \"owner request: 'svelte, go は古いので prune, typescript, python は cljc に移行して, py, ts は除去'\",
    :fact-check {:svelte \"5.0.0 (@sveltejs/kit ^2.0.0) — current major, not legacy\",
                 :go \"1.25.0 — current stable, not legacy\",
                 :verdict \"'古いので' premise does not hold; framed as architecture-unification decision instead\"},
    :inventory {:apps-server \"Go, ConnectRPC (proto/storyboard.proto + storyboardpbconnect), real Dapr actors/workflows/activities (internal/dapr/{actors,workflows,activities}.go), cuelang used for real (see addenda — corrected from initial vestigial-suspicion)\",
                :apps-web \"Svelte 5 + SvelteKit 2, ConnectRPC-web client, Lexical rich-text editor, Skeleton UI, Melt UI\",
                :apps-image-gen \"Python, 3 files\",
                :dir-260122-presentation \"Svelte/Vite presentation app, purpose unaudited\",
                :dir-260123-jump \".edn x142, pure story/character data, not executable code — out of scope\",
                :cljc-clj-cljs-count 0 :datascript-datomic-count 0},
    :feasibility {:image-gen \"HIGH — direct precedent this session: mangaka.comfy/render-via-murakumo (cloud-murakumo native ComfyUI protocol), merged gftdcojp/ai-gftd-mangaka PR\",
                  :dapr-actors-workflows \"LOW/UNKNOWN — no cljc-native distributed actor/workflow runtime exists in this monorepo; langgraph-clj StateGraph is single-process graph exec, not Dapr's distributed/sidecar model\",
                  :connectrpc \"no cljc/ClojureScript ConnectRPC implementation precedent in this monorepo\",
                  :lexical-richtext \"no cljc/ClojureScript equivalent exists\",
                  :skeleton-melt-ui \"theoretically replaceable by kotoba-ui, but moot while Lexical dependency remains\"},
    :decision {:do-now \"migrate apps/image-gen (3 python files) to cljc + cloud-murakumo; remove those 3 .py files only after migration lands\",
               :do-not \"delete apps/server (Go) or apps/web (Svelte) wholesale — no working cljc replacement exists for Dapr actors/workflows, ConnectRPC service, or Lexical editor; deleting now would destroy working storyboard-editor backend+frontend with no replacement\",
               :follow-up \"a future ADR must first settle (a) cljc-native Dapr actor/workflow replacement and (b) Lexical-equivalent rich-text editing, before any further Go/Svelte pruning is considered\",
               :side-note \"apps/server's cuelang dependency has zero .cue files in-repo — flagged as possibly vestigial, not itself a decision of this ADR\"}}",
  :adr/addenda
  [{:date "2026-07-13"
    :trigger "owner request: 'apps image gen も kotoba-lang orgs に共通 lib として設計, 移行'"
    :discovery "kotoba-lang/murakumo (the murakumo-family common lib, ADR-2607041302) already has murakumo.infer.media + murakumo.infer.gateway implementing exactly this — SSH-dispatched ComfyUI render farm with real crash-recovery (consecutive-miss detection, /queue cross-check for a crashed-and-respawned ComfyUI process that lost its in-memory queue/history — the same class of gad crash diagnosed live this same day in the ai-gftd-mangaka session)"
    :corrected-decision "apps/image-gen-clj now delegates fleet dispatch to kotoba-lang/murakumo (murakumo.infer.media/.gateway/.fleet/.schedule) instead of calling gftdcojp/cloud-murakumo directly — removes duplicated retry/job-building logic"
    :fleet-change "registered gad in kotoba-lang/murakumo's fleet.edn (wasn't a fleet member before; scheduler would have picked a Mac mini at ~3min/image instead of gad's ~20s) and fixed a comfyui/ vs ComfyUI/ scp path-casing bug specific to gad's case-sensitive Linux filesystem (symlink fix on gad itself, no code change)"
    :verified "murakumo.infer.gateway/generate-image! end-to-end: scheduler correctly picked gad, 21s, real image, correct dims/style composition"}
   {:date "2026-07-13"
    :trigger "follow-up close-out: verify the cuelang vestigial-dependency suspicion flagged in the original decision"
    :finding "cuelang is NOT vestigial — real, direct (non-indirect) go.mod dep, actually imported and used. internal/schema/storyboard.cue.go embeds the CUE schema as a Go string literal (StoryboardSchema, GetSchema() cue.Value) rather than a standalone .cue file — that's why the original 'zero .cue files' check found nothing; it checked the wrong artifact. internal/service/storyboard.go's validateAndLoad genuinely runs cueCtx.CompileBytes -> Unify(schema) -> Validate(cue.Final()) on storyboard JSON at runtime."
    :correction "do NOT remove cuelang / do NOT run go mod tidy on this dep — would break the build and remove real schema validation. Follow-up item closed."}
   {:date "2026-07-13"
    :trigger "owner request: 'next, 移行を進めて, cue も除去して, edn, cljs のみで ok' — replace cuelang (confirmed real, not vestigial) with EDN+cljs rather than leaving it in place"
    :implementation "ported all 15+ CUE type defs (#Storyboard/#Episode/#Panel/#Dialogue/etc.) to kotoba-lang/spec (EDN data + pure cljs/cljc validate/explain, no clojure.spec/malli dep, portable to kotoba-WASM) as apps/server/scripts/validate_storyboard.cljs (nbb-run); validateAndLoad now shells out to it instead of calling cuelang in-process; cuelang.org/go removed via go mod tidy, storyboard.cue.go deleted"
    :union-types "kotoba-lang/spec has no :or/:union primitive yet — modeled #Panel and #BilingualText via the :fn predicate escape hatch (try each shape, valid if either passes)"
    :documented-simplifications "#Context's pinned CUE string-literal values (JSON-LD namespace URIs) validate as plain :string (structural) rather than exact-literal; CUE 2-tuples ([int,int]) validate element type via :vector/:of but not fixed arity=2 — kotoba-lang/spec has no fixed-length vector primitive"
    :verified "go build + go vet clean; go mod tidy removed cuelang with no other usage found; two new Go tests (storyboard_validate_test.go) exercise the real nbb subprocess against valid/invalid fixtures, both pass"}
   {:date "2026-07-13/14"
    :trigger "owner correction: 'ok, では 移行済みであれば lexical, dapar, connect は除去してok' — conditional removal (if already dead/migrated elsewhere), not a blind cljs reimplementation, after investigation showed the original 'do-not-delete, no cljc replacement exists' premise (this ADR's :decision :do-not) no longer matched reality"
    :correction-of-original-decision "the original :do-not premise assumed apps/server's Dapr/ConnectRPC and apps/web's Lexical editor were load-bearing. Investigation found otherwise: apps/web's live UI already bypassed apps/server's ConnectRPC entirely (fetch-based client against apps/web/src/lib/server/* instead); apps/server's Dapr autopilot workflow was already unreachable (ChatPanel.svelte called 6 client methods, e.g. startAutonomousGeneration, that don't exist on the real fetch client); Lexical's LexicalSceneEditor.svelte had zero mount points anywhere (data never left localStorage)"
    :removed ["apps/server: internal/dapr/{activities,actors,workflows}.go" "internal/service/*.go (9 files)" "internal/mcp/server.go" "internal/jsonld/" "proto/{storyboard.proto,storyboard.pb.go,storyboardpbconnect/}" "scripts/validate_storyboard.cljs (only consumer removed)" "cmd/server/main.go" "apps/dapr/components/statestore.yaml" "apps/web: LexicalSceneEditor.svelte, lexical/KindleNodes.ts, 7 lexical + 2 connectrpc npm deps"]
        :kept "cmd/mcp-cursor, cmd/indexer (both independent binaries, zero dependency on removed code); @bufbuild/protobuf (re-added after removal broke manga-layouts.ts, which 10 live Storyboard components use for local schema construction unrelated to RPC)"
        :verified "go build/vet/test clean, go mod tidy removed connectrpc.com/connect + dapr/go-sdk + protobuf cleanly; tsc --noEmit error set byte-identical before/after (64 errors, same codes)"
        :also-corrected "README's separate 2026-06 claim that kami-app-sip-clj superseded this pipeline was also wrong — that project moved to orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-sip and is a read-only storyboard reader (no save/edit/RPC/chat/PDF/job-queue), not a functional replacement. The real current authoring workflow is hand-edited EDN under org-spirit-in-physics-comics/ rendered by a babashka static-site generator, independent of both."}
       {:date "2026-07-14"
        :trigger "owner request: '1,2,3,4' — four follow-up cleanup items identified after the addendum-3 retirement"
        :item-1 "deleted internal/resolver/hybrid.go + internal/vectors/store.go — zero consumers in apps/server both before and after addendum 3 (pre-existing dead code, not a byproduct of the retirement itself); go build/vet/test clean, no go.mod/go.sum change"
        :item-2 "ChatPanel.svelte: removed UI/handlers calling the 6 nonexistent storyboardClient methods (getChatSessions/saveChatSession/analyzeStructure/interactWithAI/startAutonomousGeneration/terminateAutonomousGeneration — would TypeError at runtime); kept the message-list shell and the one real feature (/avatar shortcut via generatePanelImage); added compatible no-op/minimal stub exports (triggerAgent/addMessage/addContext) so StoryboardEditor.svelte's bind:this calls into it don't crash; removed the now-dead onApplyPatches prop/handler (interactWithAI-backed patches never worked since that client method never existed)"
        :item-3 "storyboard_pb.ts: 2688 lines (protobuf-es v2 codegen for the full retired 27-RPC-method proto) trimmed to 394 lines covering only the 7 message types (Panel/PanelData/Dialogue/GeneratedImage/MangaLayout/MangaPanelLayout/MangaText) that apps/web's Storyboard components actually use as local TS data shapes post-RPC-retirement; regenerated via a scoped buf.gen.yaml (ES/TS plugin only, deliberately omitting the original config's Go/ConnectRPC plugins) against a minimal proto carrying the same field names/numbers/types for shape compatibility"
        :item-4 "README: removed the Neo4j/producer/(Next.js)/tRPC/Wattpad-CLI/roadmap-checklist prose that had been flagged stale since the 2026-07-10 addendum-1 correction but never actually deleted; replaced with an accurate description of the current apps/web + apps/image-gen-clj + apps/server(cmd/mcp-cursor,cmd/indexer only) + org-spirit-in-physics-comics layout"
        :verified "go build/vet/test clean; tsc --noEmit error set byte-identical to a fresh clone of main (20 errors, same file:code pairs); svelte-check: 8 fewer errors than baseline (ChatPanel's dead calls resolved), zero new ones — confirmed via normalized file:line diff against baseline, including after fixing one initially-introduced regression (StoryboardEditor.svelte's onApplyPatches prop reference) caught by svelte-check but invisible to plain tsc --noEmit (chatPanel ref is typed any)"}]}]
